  "summary": "Earliest time you can swim from corner to corner as water rises.",
  "statement": "`grid[i][j]` is the elevation of each cell (all values are distinct, `0..n*n-1`). At time `t` the water\ndepth is `t`, and you can move between neighboring cells (up/down/left/right) if both have elevation at\nmost `t`. Return the earliest time you can get from the top-left to the bottom-right.",
