  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public int swimInWater(int[][] grid) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return 0;\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "The time for a path is the highest cell on it. You want the path whose highest cell is lowest.",
    "Dijkstra where a path's cost is the max elevation so far, always expanding the lowest-cost cell first.",
    "pq = [(grid[0][0], 0, 0)]\nseen = {(0, 0)}\nwhile pq:\n    t, r, c = pop min\n    if (r, c) is the goal: return t\n    for unvisited neighbors: mark; push (max(t, grid[nr][nc]), nr, nc)",
    "A min-heap on max-elevation-so-far gives O(n^2 log n). Binary search on t with a flood-fill check also works."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(n^2 log n)",
    "space": "O(n^2)"
  },
